  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1...\n\nHigh pressure across the area will provide drier weather to the \narea. A few passing disturbances will trigger isolated showers \nFriday, with isolated to scattered convection expected for Saturday \nand Sunday as additional disturbances cross the area. At this point, \nstorms over the weekend are not looking to be severe. Focus then \nshifts towards Sunday night into early next week, in which a series \nof convective disturbances look to form across the midwest and drop \nsoutheast into our area. These could bring a damaging wind and heavy \nrain threat to our region, but overall, the exact details are \nuncertain at this point. SPC has an area just to the west of our CWA \nalready outlooked for day 5 for the potential of severe weather.",
